{% if task.target_stage == "first_pass" %}
### Required Actions (Stage 1: First-Pass Research)

1. **Research Project & Gather Sources:**
   Gather verified project details and exact verbatim source quotes from the official repository and documentation.
   Write or enrich structured research YAML at:
   `{{ task.research_file }}`

   Schema:
   ```yaml
   project_name: "{{ task.project_name }}"
   homepage_url: "{{ task.homepage_url or '' }}"
   repo_url: "{{ task.repo_url or '' }}"
   cncf_status: "{{ task.cncf_status }}"
   summary: ""
   key_features:
     - ""
   recent_updates: ""
   use_cases: ""
   interesting_facts: ""
   get_started: ""
   related_tools:
     - ""
   sources:
     - id: "src_readme"
       title: "GitHub README"
       url: "{{ task.repo_url or '' }}"
       source_type: "github_readme"
       quotes:
         - "Verbatim excerpt from official source grounding summary/features"
   last_researched_at: "<ISO 8601 UTC>"
   research_version: 1
   ```

2. **Update Week Tracker (Research Task Only):**
   In `{{ task.tracker_file }}`, locate `{{ task.project_name }}` and update ONLY the research task:
   - `tasks.research.status: completed`
   - `tasks.research.output_file: {{ task.research_file }}`
   - `tasks.research.completed_at: <ISO 8601 UTC>`
   - **Leave `tasks.content.status: pending`** (do NOT mark completed).

### Strict Guardrails (First Pass)
- **DO NOT generate or create the Hugo tool page (`{{ task.tool_page_file }}`) in this PR.**
- **DO NOT mark `tasks.content` completed in the tracker.**
- CI enforces strict single-step lifecycle transitions (`initial -> first_pass`). Any PR attempting to skip directly to `tech_writing` or creating `{{ task.tool_page_file }}` will be blocked by `validate_contract.py`.
- Deliver ONLY the research YAML and the tracker research task update in this PR.

{% elif task.target_stage == "tech_writing" %}
